From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] omcproxy: retain downlinks present in replacement configuration

The replacement-config scan stops at the first different interface index
instead of at a matching index. It can remove retained downlinks or keep
an absent one according to list order. Search until a match is found and
remove a downlink only when the complete replacement list lacks its index.
Keep the existing querier/client/MRIB teardown and creation owners.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/src/proxy.c
+++ b/src/proxy.c
@@ -162,7 +162,7 @@ int proxy_set(int uplink, const int down
 		struct querier_user_iface *iface = container_of(user, struct querier_user_iface, user);
 
 		size_t i;
-		for (i = 0; i < downlinks_cnt && downlinks[i] == iface->iface->ifindex; ++i);
+		for (i = 0; i < downlinks_cnt && downlinks[i] != iface->iface->ifindex; ++i);
 		if (i == downlinks_cnt)
 			proxy_remove_downlink(container_of(iface, struct proxy_downlink, iface));
 	}
